      "sourceUrl": "https://markitai.com/u/jonathan/e/lNlfA5LPaM",
      "startsAt": "2026-11-07T01:00:00.000Z",
      "status": "CONFIRMED",
      "summary": "Boston Founder House Party",
      "timezone": "America/Detroit",
      "uid": "markit:lNlfA5LPaM",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-31T05:30:58.651Z",
      "description": "SF founders throw house parties on Friday nights. Boston founders network on Tuesdays at 6pm. Let's change that.\nAfter a few weeks out in SF, I'm throwing the first Boston founder house party. When I posted about this on\nLinkedIn\nand\nInstagram\n, it went semi-viral. It got 70K+ impressions and a flood of DMs from people asking when it was happening. Everyone was begging for it, so we decided to actually do something about it.\nSo here it is. We're keeping the first one small and bringing together a hand-picked group of Boston's best founders and builders for a Friday night where you can actually let loose. If this becomes a thing, you'll want to say you were at the first one.\nBella Pivo and I are hosting it at her apartment in Cambridge. The exact address goes out to approved guests.\nSpace is very limited and every guest is approved by hand. If there's someone you think should be there, message one of us!\nBig thanks to our partner\nFidelity Private Shares\nfor supporting the party and bringing fun to Boston!.\n​Fidelity Private Shares is committed to supporting the startup & venture capital community. Fidelity helps founders prepare for their next round of funding with our\ncap table management and data room platform\n, events that give you access to seed stage capital, equity scenario modeling, and premier support to generate, execute & store legal documents.  No matter where you are in your journey - from inception to IPO - Fidelity has the expertise to support you."
    },
